From cbb6d74ecfd33bc138b5afd5ebc567eeee24e349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:25:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): keep the conversation TTS lease held across
 tile mount/unmount

Every mounted composer (the main chat bar and each session tile) runs
useComposerVoice against the same per-renderer CONVERSATION_LEASE, and
tts-lease.ts dedupes on one module-level "last sent" value. The acquire
effect and the unmount cleanup were unconditional, so a tile mounting or
unmounting while another composer's voice conversation was active sent
syncTtsLease(CONVERSATION_LEASE, false) and released the lease
mid-conversation. The backend then unloads resident local TTS models
(piper/kittentts), so the next spoken reply pays the cold load the lease
exists to hide, and the owner's own end-of-conversation release is
deduped away.

Track ownership with a ref, mirroring ownsWakeIndicatorRef: only the
composer that acquired the lease releases it (on end or unmount). The
test mounts real useComposerVoice instances against the real tts-lease
module with only the wire call stubbed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
